{"base_rate":0.3080110497237569,"brier":0.156935635359116,"bss":0.263697773958809,"bss_hi":0.41944217890480817,"bss_lo":0.09519389703165351,"chart":{"base":[328.3,173.5],"fp":[197.9,121.9],"lead":"62,227.9 272,200.1 482,189.7 692,186.5","note":{"base":"skill 0.26 — higher than 40% of cities","fp":"low end -1pp, high end +28pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.3 °C — better than 24% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 1%; promised 100% → rained 84%"},"rel":"70.6,461.4 339.4,388.8 608.3,257.6 690.5,101.6"},"country":"BD","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.16571823204419883,"ess":220.47304380381695,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Rangpur</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Rangpur rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>84%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>0%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 724 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 2.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.26, ranked 129 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(48&ndash;178) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>0%</b></td><td class='num'>217</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>59%</td><td class='num'><b>26%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>80%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>92%</td><td class='num'><b>60%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>84%</b></td><td class='num'>147</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Rangpur</b> <span class=\"muted\">Bangladesh</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;31% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 31% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.26</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>48&ndash;178\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>724 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Rangpur &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Rangpur\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 78.70363636363636,337.8787878787879 161.30363636363637,240.1818181818182 268.5343243243243,126.2162162162162 341.0910769230769,57.19999999999999 384.8599999999999,27.333333333333314 411.1330612244897,18.0 411.1330612244897,22.952380952380963 384.8599999999999,69.33333333333337 341.0910769230769,124.39999999999998 268.5343243243243,204.9189189189189 161.30363636363637,311.0909090909091 78.70363636363636,376.4848484848485 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"269.8839779005525\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"269.8839779005525\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,380.3225806451613 78.70363636363636,370.969696969697 161.30363636363637,344.1818181818182 268.5343243243243,288.5405405405405 341.0910769230769,258.8 384.8599999999999,162.66666666666669 411.1330612244897,74.95238095238096\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 0% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 217 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"380.3225806451613\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 6%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"78.70363636363636\" cy=\"370.969696969697\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 29%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"161.30363636363637\" cy=\"344.1818181818182\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 59%&amp;#10;It rained 26% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"268.5343243243243\" cy=\"288.5405405405405\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 80%&amp;#10;It rained 34% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 65 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"341.0910769230769\" cy=\"258.8\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 92%&amp;#10;It rained 60% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"384.8599999999999\" cy=\"162.66666666666669\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 84% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 147 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.1330612244897\" cy=\"74.95238095238096\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(31%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Rangpur the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.23) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.37).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'>-0.366</td><td class='num'>1.6%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>169</td><td class='num'>59%</td><td class='num'>-0.071</td><td class='num'>27.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'>0.057</td><td class='num'>21.1%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>206</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.233</td><td class='num'>16.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":25.74664,"lon":89.25166,"n":724,"n_cities":216,"name":"Rangpur","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.018000000000000682,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":217,"obs":0.004608294930875576,"sig":true},{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.018000000000000682,"mean":0.05848484848484848,"n":66,"obs":0.030303030303030304,"sig":false},{"hi":0.47,"lo":0.14,"mean":0.2918181818181818,"n":77,"obs":0.1038961038961039,"sig":true},{"hi":0.7260000000000013,"lo":0.47,"mean":0.5947297297297296,"n":74,"obs":0.25675675675675674,"sig":true},{"hi":0.88,"lo":0.7260000000000013,"mean":0.7996923076923077,"n":65,"obs":0.3384615384615385,"sig":true},{"hi":0.97,"lo":0.88,"mean":0.9233333333333331,"n":78,"obs":0.6025641025641025,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.97,"mean":0.9975510204081631,"n":147,"obs":0.8435374149659864,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":2.4,"provisional":false,"rank":129,"rank_hi":178.02499999999998,"rank_lo":48.0,"reliability":0.05050991110625836,"resolution":0.10698011546841898,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"rangpur","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Dhaka"